# Without this, `COPY engine/ ./engine/` etc. in the Dockerfile would copy
# each subproject's HOST-MACHINE node_modules directly on top of the ones
# the image just installed fresh with `npm install --prefix <dir> --omit=dev`
# — shipping wrong-platform native binaries (e.g. macOS-built sharp/appium
# bits into this Linux image) and pulling in devDependencies the image was
# never supposed to have. Found while verifying the Docker build actually
# works end to end, not just that the Dockerfile parses.
**/node_modules

.git
.github
.env
*.log
/generated
/docs
README.md
